 "notes": "The Bluff Point corner of Gubal Seghir, the standard overnight mooring: the light, the wall where the current wraps round the point, and the Barge (about 35 x 6 m, 14 m) in the sheltered bay. Shore, reef edge, light and the Barge position come from OpenStreetMap, the Barge size and depth from the Red Sea Wreck Project; the lagoon is the shallow strip between the reef edge and the shore. The drift line is the usual wall drift from the point to the mooring, not a recorded track; positions are approximate.",
